From bb224617d7bc525fcd9ad05424c104adacf37b1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thc1006 <84045975+thc1006@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 07:51:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] tests : show that a batch of interleaved sequences gives
 unsorted out_ids

output_reorder() only does work when out_ids come back out of order: output_swaps is built inside
`if (!sorted_output && n_outputs > 1)`. Nothing in the suite reached that state, so the buffers it
permutes were never exercised through it.

Interleaving two sequences and requesting an output on every token is enough. split_equal groups
by sequence, so the outputs come back as batch indices 0, 2, 1, 3 and out_ids is not the identity.

Signed-off-by: thc1006 <84045975+thc1006@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 tests/test-batch-alloc.cpp | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/test-batch-alloc.cpp b/tests/test-batch-alloc.cpp
index 66d29d6..0ac9318 100644
--- a/tests/test-batch-alloc.cpp
+++ b/tests/test-batch-alloc.cpp
@@ -349,6 +349,42 @@ static void test_split(testing & t) {
         t.assert_equal(3u, ub.n_tokens);
     });
 
+    // Reaching an unsorted out_ids is what makes llama_context::output_reorder() do any work at
